For the protons and leptons, that interact with the B-field, the density is given by

\\rho_{i}=\\frac{|q|B}{2\\pi^{2}}\\sum_{\\nu=0}^{\\nu_{\\rm max}^{i}}\\sum_{s}k_{i, \\nu s}^{F}\\,,  with i=p,l, where \\nu=n+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{q}{|q|}s=0,1,\\cdots,\\nu_{\\rm max} enumerates the Landau levels (LLs) for fermions with electric charge q, \\nu_{\\rm max} is the largest LL occupied by fully degenerate charged fermions, defined as

